  "optimized_instruction": "Analyze the chronological 15-frame storyboard (approximately 0\u201314 seconds, ordered left-to-right and top-to-bottom) together with its aligned commentary. Identify exactly one dominant event that actually occurs in this clip.\n\nFirst trace the full sequence: setup \u2192 decisive action or referee decision \u2192 visible outcome. Treat commentary only as supporting evidence because it may be early, delayed, or refer to prior play. Do not count a replay, recap, repeated angle, celebration, or retrospective commentary as a new event.\n\nChoose exactly one label:\n- kickoff: play starts or a half restarts from the center circle; do not use for other restarts.\n- goal: strong evidence shows the ball crossed the line and the goal was awarded, such as the ball in the net, score change, referee confirmation, aligned commentary, or sustained celebration.\n- penalty: a penalty is clearly awarded, prepared, or taken; contact in the box alone is insufficient. If the kick\u2019s outcome is shown, label goal, miss, or shot instead.\n- red card: a sending-off is visibly shown or explicitly confirmed, including a second yellow leading to dismissal.\n- yellow card: a booking is visibly shown or explicitly confirmed; a foul or referee confrontation alone is insufficient.\n- corner: a corner is clearly awarded or taken. If it leads to a visible attempt in the clip, label the attempt\u2019s later outcome instead.\n- miss: an intentional attempt is completed and clearly finishes off target (wide, over, or otherwise missing). Establish both attempt and outcome.\n- shot: an intentional attempt is completed and is saved, blocked, on target, or has an unresolved final outcome. Do not confuse crosses, passes, clearances, or attacking buildup with shots.\n- no important event: no listed event is established with adequate evidence.\n\nIf multiple labels apply to the same sequence, use this priority:\ngoal > red card > yellow card > penalty > miss > shot > corner > kickoff > no important event.\n\nReturn:\n- event_type: exactly one label above.\n- time_in_clip_sec: the approximate time of the decisive action or confirmed outcome, from 0 to 15; use -1 only for no important event. For a miss, prefer when the off-target outcome becomes clear; for a goal, prefer when scoring is confirmed; for cards or penalties, prefer the referee decision or visible confirmation.\n- confidence: a number from 0.0 to 1.0, reduced when the action, outcome, or replay status is ambiguous.\n- evidence: one or two short, factual observations grounded in the storyboard and/or transcript. Do not add unsupported details.",
